977. Squares of a Sorted Array

Given an integer array nums sorted in non-decreasing order, return an array of the squares of each number sorted in non-decreasing order.

Explaantion:

This is a 2pointer problem
keep a ans array with left and pos index to traverse
trvaerse from left <=right
take the number on the left and take a number on right
check if abs(left)>abs(right)
if so add the square of left on the last part of the ans array and l++- cause we need to return the sorted array
the biggest element goes into the end
likewise check and do for nums[r] > nums[l] with r++

and then move the pos index one step back



Code:
class Solution {
    public int[] sortedSquares(int[] nums) {
        int left=0; int right=nums.length-1;
        int[] ans = new int[nums.length];
        int pos=nums.length-1;;

        while(left<=right){
            int numL = nums[left];
            int numR = nums[right];
            if(Math.abs(numL) >= Math.abs(numR)){
                ans[pos] = numL * numL;
                left++;
            }
            else if(Math.abs(numL) < Math.abs(numR)){
                ans[pos] = numR* numR;
                right--;
            }
            pos--;
        }
        return ans;
    }
}
